---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Azure Architecture • AI Engineering • Business Automation</p>
      <h1>Secure Azure and AI systems—from focused automation to enterprise-scale platforms.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Archytum combines senior architecture guidance, hands-on AI engineering, and human-controlled automation to build the right level of solution for each business.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button teal" href="/contact/?path=enterprise">Discuss an Azure or AI initiative</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/business-ai/">Explore small-business AI packages</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="trust-strip" aria-label="Archytum operating principles">
    <div class="container trust-grid">
      <div class="trust-item">Clear scope</div>
      <div class="trust-item">Measurable outcomes</div>
      <div class="trust-item">Human approval where consequences matter</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Choose your path</p>
        <h2>Right-sized help for the system you need now.</h2>
        <p>Start with a focused operating workflow or engage senior architecture leadership for a complex Azure and AI initiative.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="tag">Small and growing businesses</span>
          <h2>Business AI Solutions</h2>
          <p>Turn everyday email, calendar, follow-up, and operating work into reliable, human-approved systems.</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Microsoft 365 workflow automation</li>
            <li>Daily action briefs and meeting preparation</li>
            <li>Predictable implementation and monthly tiers</li>
          </ul>
          <p><a class="link" href="/business-ai/">Explore Business AI →</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="tag">Growing and enterprise organizations</span>
          <h2>Enterprise Azure & AI</h2>
          <p>Design and deliver secure cloud foundations, AI platforms, integrations, and architecture at enterprise scale.</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Architecture assessment and strategy</li>
            <li>Fractional principal-architect leadership</li>
            <li>Platform engineering and delivery</li>
          </ul>
          <p><a class="link" href="/enterprise-azure-ai/">Explore Enterprise services →</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How Archytum works</p>
        <h2>Evidence before expansion.</h2>
        <p>Every engagement begins with the business outcome and a bounded scope. Permissions, automation, and spend expand only when evidence supports them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-4 process">
        <article class="card"><h3>Clarify</h3><p>Define the decision, workflow, risk, or measurable outcome.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Assess</h3><p>Map the current state, constraints, data boundaries, and tradeoffs.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Deliver</h3><p>Build the smallest complete path with acceptance criteria and evidence.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Improve</h3><p>Measure results, correct failure modes, and expand deliberately.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p>
        <h2>Useful automation without invisible authority.</h2>
        <p>AI can prepare, summarize, detect, and draft. People retain approval over messages, meetings, public claims, contracts, payments, and consequential changes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="metric"><strong>Read first</strong><span>Separate observation and analysis from write access.</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>Trace the source</strong><span>Keep evidence, uncertainty, and decision history visible.</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>Fail closed</strong><span>Stop when identity, scope, permission, or confirmation is unclear.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">First case study</p>
        <h2>Archytum is building its own operating system first.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The Inbox-to-Action system is being designed around Archytum’s Microsoft 365 environment: read-only email and calendar intake, a prioritized daily brief, meeting preparation, and an approval queue.</p>
        <p><strong>Status:</strong> case study in progress. Results will be published only after representative operation and measurable evidence.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/work/inbox-to-action/">See the case-study design</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
